{
  "dom_id": "step-q109594",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Find the surface area of the part of the plane $z=2x+3y$ that is bounded by the constraints $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $1\\le y\\le 3.$",
  "worked_solution": "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=f(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\u222c}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={\u222c}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\u2202z}{\u2202x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\u2202z}{\u2202y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nz=2x+3y,\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 3.\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202z}{\u2202x} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(2x+3y)=2, \\\\ \\frac{\u2202z}{\u2202y} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(2x+3y)=3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={\u222c}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\u2202z}{\u2202x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\u2202z}{\u2202y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}\\sqrt{1+(2)^{2}+(3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}\\sqrt{1+4+9}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}\\sqrt{14}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}{\u222c}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}\\cdot (1-0)\\cdot (3-1) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
